.pdxdoc-tool pkg
.pdxdoc-tool-version 1.0.0
.pdxdoc-tool-repo https://github.com/paideia-os/pkg
.pdxdoc-tool-wave R49
.pdxdoc-tool-milestone M5
.pdxdoc-format-notes This file is consumed by the `doc` tool
  (github.com/paideia-os/doc). Sections are blank-line-separated.
  Section headers are ALL-CAPS on a line by themselves. Bullets are
  hyphen-prefixed. Cross-references use the `see:<tool>` marker,
  parsed by doc.M3+ into hyperlink records. See
  design/release-1.0.md §7 for the format rationale.

NAME

pkg -- paideia-os package manager. Installs, upgrades, removes,
lists, and audits signed tool packages from pkgs.paideia-os and
mirrors; the tool that bootstraps every other tool in the R49/R50
waves.

SYNOPSIS

pkg <subcommand> [<flags>] [<arguments>]

Subcommands (M5 vocabulary):
- install <name>                 -- install a signed package
- remove  <name>                 -- remove an installed package (undo-journalled)
- list    [--available]          -- list installed (or available) packages
- verify  <name>                 -- re-verify an installed package's signatures
- keys    list                   -- list the signing keys pkg trusts

pkg --help                       -- print usage + one line per subcommand
pkg --version                    -- print "pkg 1.0.0"

--help and --version are wired at the top level (ENH-006 #31): they
short-circuit before subcommand dispatch and work with or without a
subcommand or positional argument present. No other flag has a body
wired at 1.0.0 (see README.md's capabilities section and ENH-002 for
the reserved-but-unwired I3 vocabulary).

DESCRIPTION

pkg is the R49 wave package manager. Every tool in the paideia-os
tooling ecosystem ships as a dual-signed package; pkg is the tool
that fetches, verifies, and installs them, and the first tool that
bootstraps itself by running `pkg install pkg` against a from-source
build.

The install pipeline is 4 stages, sequenced in
src/install.pdx per design/install-flow.md §3:

- FETCH: acquire the package manifest + tar from the mirror.
- VERIFY: dual ML-DSA-65 signature verify (author + paideia-root),
  sha3-256 body-hash cross-check, per-file inventory hash check.
- UNPACK: extract the tar into a KIND_PDXFS_TXN scope so a partial
  install rolls back cleanly.
- RENAME: atomically move the extracted tree into /pkgs/<name>-
  <version>/ and update /system/packages/index.pdxlist.

Verification is all-or-nothing: no output byte reaches the user
until both signatures verify. This is the D4 audit-first discipline
in the r49-r50-plan.md.

SUBCOMMANDS

install <name>
  Fetch, verify, and install <name> from the currently-configured
  mirror. Acquires KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write,/pkgs) for a 60s window
  via libpdx-elevate (see src/pkg_elevate.pdx). Refuses if either
  signature fails, if the body-hash mismatches the header, or if
  the caps.decl hash in the manifest does not match the caps.decl
  packaged in the tar. Emits an InstallProgressRecord per stage on
  the semantic pipe (pdxsig.pkg.ipr.v1 schema).

remove <name>
  Remove an installed package. Writes an undo record to /journal/
  pkg/ so `undo pkg install <name>` reconstructs the install from
  the trash-subtree entry. `--wipe` shreds the trash entry
  immediately (audit-flagged as unrecoverable). Removes from
  /system/packages/index.pdxlist.

list [--available]
  Without --available, walks /system/packages/ and prints one line
  per installed package. With --available, queries the current
  mirror for its full package index and prints one line per
  available package. Emits PackageManifest records on the
  semantic pipe (pdxsig.pkg.pmf.v1 schema).

verify <name>
  Re-verify an already-installed package's signatures against the
  packaged manifest.pdxsig. Does not touch the network; the
  manifest travels with the install. Useful after a
  paideia_root_pk rotation to confirm every installed package
  still verifies under the new fingerprint.

keys list
  List the signing keys pkg trusts. Reads /system/keys/
  paideia_root_pk.fpr and prints the sha3-256 fingerprint per key
  in ml-dsa-65 format. See release/1.0/keys-fingerprints.md in
  the pkg repo for the fingerprint discipline.

CAPS

Baseline (loader-seeded via InitCap sidecar):
- KIND_USER (self)                            -- identity root
- KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT (invoke)                  -- pipe substrate
- KIND_PDXFS_FILE (read, /system/packages/)   -- package enumeration
- KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL (invoke, svc.elevate-broker)  -- per-install
                                                        elevate flow

Per-install (acquired via libpdx-elevate for a 60s window):
- KIND_PDXFS_FILE (write, /pkgs)              -- install destination
- KIND_NETWORK   (fetch, pkgs.paideia-os)     -- mirror fetch
- KIND_SIGNATURE (verify, paideia_root_pk)    -- sig-verify

pkg NEVER runs with ambient write authority on /pkgs/. Write caps
are acquired per-install via the elevate broker per D4
discipline. See caps.decl in the pkg repo for the full manifest.

EXAMPLES

Install ls (the coreutils listing tool):
  pkg install ls
  # -> InstallProgressRecord[RESOLVED, VERIFIED_AUTHOR,
  #                          VERIFIED_ROOT, CAP_AUDIT, INSTALLED]
  # -> exit 0

List installed packages:
  pkg list
  # -> PackageManifest records: pkg, ls, cat, doc, ...
  # -> exit 0

Verify an installed package:
  pkg verify pkg
  # -> InstallProgressRecord[VERIFIED_AUTHOR, VERIFIED_ROOT]
  # -> exit 0

Remove a package (undo-journalled):
  pkg remove ls
  # -> writes /journal/pkg/undo-<ts>.record
  # -> `undo pkg install ls` reconstructs the install
  # -> exit 0

List signing keys:
  pkg keys list
  # -> paideia_root  ml-dsa-65  <fingerprint>  (rotated: never)
  # -> pkg-author    ml-dsa-65  <fingerprint>  (rotated: never)
  # -> exit 0

Semantic-pipe filter (e.g. installed packages authored by <fpr>):
  pkg list | query "PackageManifest.author_fpr == '<fpr>'"

Cross-boundary install (elevate to /system/):
  pkg install --dest /system/tools some-tool
  # -> libpdx-elevate prompts the founder via svc.elevate-broker
  # -> InstallProgressRecord[ELEVATE_PENDING, ELEVATE_APPROVED, ...]

